# Working notes and investigations that are not part of the
# published project: thinking-in-progress, findings not yet
# decided upon, material we may or may not act on.
# Working files only: one-shot patch scripts, scratch, and the
# rolling session handover. The process RECORDS are published in
# docs/process/ -- campaigns, findings, the note sent upstream. What
# stays here is what has no reader but the next session.
dev/

# Agent worktrees live inside the repo directory. Git skips a
# registered worktree, but an unregistered leftover would be
# swept in by the release's git add -A, which commits a whole
# second copy of the project.
.claude/worktrees/

# Build products and generated evidence. Reports are attached to
# GitHub Releases instead of committed: they run to tens of megabytes
# per version, and git keeps every blob forever.
dist/
reports/
.venv-reference/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Never committed, for privacy rather than secrecy: the private style
# guide that governs this project's prose lives outside the repository,
# and these names are listed so a stray copy cannot arrive by accident.
bergmann-osullivan-voice-dna.md
anti-ai-writing-style.md

# Credentials, in every shape they usually take. tools/check_no_secrets.py
# is the real guard; this is the belt to its braces.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*_rsa
*_ed25519
.netrc

# Claude Code writes local permission state here, with absolute paths
# from this machine. Local to a checkout, never project content.
.claude/settings.local.json
